{
  "families": [
    {
      "family": "unrolled_k",
      "ranges": [
        {"param": "data_width", "low": 14, "high": 18, "choices": null},
        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 12, "high": 20, "choices": null},
        {"param": "k", "low": 2, "high": 8, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": -1, "high": 3, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 3, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]}
      ],
      "budget_share": 0.90,
      "why": "Only family of mine that can plausibly reach the ~64 msps burst rate: k chained micro-rotations cut cycles/result to ceil(N/k)+3 while keeping one shared datapath. Sweep k 2..8 to find the Fmax-vs-cycles optimum, N 12..20 and W 14..18 to trace the accuracy/area front, with small guard ranges."
    },
    {
      "family": "iterative",
      "ranges": [
        {"param": "data_width", "low": 14, "high": 18, "choices": null},
        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 12, "high": 20, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": -1, "high": 3, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 3, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]}
      ],
      "budget_share": 0.10,
      "why": "Smallest area (one micro-rotation/cycle) but N+3 >= 15 cycles/result, so it needs Fmax >= ~1 GHz to meet the 0.5 us batch — implausible in sky130. Small share to confirm infeasibility and to cover the low-area corner if the analytic Fmax is generous."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The binding constraint is the system burst: 32 requests must land within 0.5 us of the tick, i.e. an effective burst throughput of ~64 msps (with margin, ~70-80). For my families throughput_msps = Fmax/(ceil(N/k)+3) (unrolled_k) or Fmax/(N+3) (iterative). Accuracy (max_abs_err <= 2^-12) forces N >= ~13 (angle residual ~2^-N) and W >= 14 (output LSB 2^-(W-2)), so I search W 14..18, N 12..20. Iterative then needs Fmax >= 64*(N+3) >= ~1 GHz, which is far beyond sky130 for a 14-bit CORDIC, so it is almost certainly infeasible; I keep a small share to confirm and to catch the low-area corner if the model is unexpectedly fast. unrolled_k needs Fmax >= 64*(ceil(N/k)+3): 320 MHz at k=8/N=16, 448 MHz at k=4, 704 MHz at k=2. Since Fmax falls with k (longer combinational chain) while cycles/result also falls, the throughput optimum is at an intermediate k, so I sweep k 2..8. Area is minimised at small W, N, k, so the front is the accuracy/throughput boundary; angle_guard and frac_guard are swept modestly because they trade a little area for internal truncation margin."
}
